# DROP YOUR SAMPLES HERE

## Expected file names (drop .mp3 or .wav into this folder):

- `tap.mp3` → UI button press (very short, ~50ms wood-knock)
- `good.mp3` → success/perfect (~400ms bright stab)
- `bad.mp3` → fail (~500ms low womp)
- `almost.mp3` → near-miss (~300ms neutral)
- `go.mp3` → start signal (~400ms ascending)
- `stop.mp3` → stop/end (~300ms descending)
- `buzzer.mp3` → wrong/timeout (~500ms harsh)
- `win.mp3` → match win fanfare (~800ms triumphant)
- `elim.mp3` → elimination (~600ms dramatic)
- `tick.mp3` → countdown tick (very short, ~30ms click)
- `whoosh.mp3` → transition wipe (~400ms swoosh)
- `confetti.mp3` → celebration burst (~600ms party)
- `coin.mp3` → coin earned (~300ms metallic)
- `streak.mp3` → streak achieved (~500ms power-up)
- `chaos.mp3` → chaos moment trigger (~600ms explosive)
- `crowd.mp3` → crowd reaction loop (~2s ambient cheering)

## Format

- **Format:** MP3 or WAV (MP3 recommended for size)
- **Bitrate:** 128 kbps is plenty for SFX
- **Mono** is fine — saves bandwidth
- **Volume:** normalize to -6dB peak so the in-game mixer can balance them

## Behavior

- App **automatically detects** files in this folder on startup
- If a sample is missing, the app falls back to the synthetic Web-Audio version
- You can drop any subset — only `tap.mp3` alone already feels great
- Files are loaded once on first user interaction (browser audio policy)

## Tips for finding samples

- **Free options:** freesound.org, pixabay.com/sound-effects, zapsplat.com
- **AI generation:** ElevenLabs Sound Effects, Suno, Stable Audio
- **Check license:** prefer CC0 / Royalty-Free for commercial use
- **Test:** drop one sample, refresh page, hear difference vs synth fallback
